{"created": "2024-02-23T19:52:12.956516+00:00", "modified": "2024-07-07T04:01:55.597373+00:00", "id": 10697026, "conceptrecid": "10697025", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10697026", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.10697025", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10697026", "metadata": {"title": "Volumetric Velocity/Pressure measurements of a supersonic Double-fin flow at M=2 and alpha=10deg", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10697026", "publication_date": "2024-02-23", "description": "<p>These are measurements of the flow over a double-fin obtained through the scanning stereoscopic PIV technique we describe here:&nbsp;https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00348-023-03596-w</p>\n<p>\"A continuously scanning spatiotemporal averaging method for obtaining volumetric mean flow measurements with stereoscopic PIV\" (Zigunov, Seckin, Huss, Eggart and Alvi, ExIF, 2022)</p>\n<p>The original and processed velocity fields are under SSPIV_Fluctuations_Run08_DF_10deg_M2.mat, along with the Reynolds stresses (although their statistical convergence is not as good).</p>\n<p>Average pressure is computed with our Omnidirectional pressure integrator (https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.16935) in the file Omnidirectional Pressure_Paraview_DF_10deg.vtk&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The geometry of the fin is also included as a STL file.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Zigunov, Fernando", "affiliation": "Florida State University"}], "contributors": [{"name": "Seckin, Serdar", "affiliation": "Florida State University", "type": "DataCollector"}], "keywords": ["particle image velocimetry", "Pressure from PIV"], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Other", "type": "other"}, "journal": {"issue": "56", "title": "Experiments In Fluids", "volume": "64"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "10697025"}}]}}, "title": "Volumetric Velocity/Pressure measurements of a supersonic Double-fin flow a